\par\par \b \uc2 Hungary's forint reverses some losses, eyes CPI.  \b0\par\par\uc2 549 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 17:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST, March 10 (Reuters) - Hungary's forint reversed some of the heavy losses suffered earlier on Thursday due to the zloty's fall and government bond prices stabilised around the lows reached in early trade, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 1615 GMT the forint was quoted at 243.20/60 to the euro, down sharply from 241.61/242.11 late on Wednesday, but firmer from the intraday peak of around 244.50.  \par \par \uc2 "The forint firmed back a little after the zloty calmed down around 3.95 (to the euro)," one dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 In early trade the forint had dropped almost one percent and yields had risen by up to 12 basis points, tracking drastic losses in Polish markets. Hungary also cut its auction of 12-month Treasury bill auction on Thursday due to low demand.  \par \par \uc2 Most traders said the falls were caused by a regional trend rather than any market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBH). The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  declined to comment.  \par \par \uc2 Bond yields stabilised in the afternoon after initial rises. Dealers expected them to be flat at the higher levels reached on Thursday or even move further up in the coming days if U.S. and euro zone government papers do not recover from recent losses.  \par \par \uc2 "Longer papers will stay at this level or weaken further and shorter ones will probably not change much," one dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The forint reversed some of the losses in vibrant trade in the afternoon, but its retreat calmed some fears of an attack on the edge of its trading band.  \par \par \uc2 "The danger that someone will use the two-day holiday to move the forint out of its trading band is now a little bit more mooted," one dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 Some analysts had expected foreign banks to use the national holiday in Hungary on March 14 and 15 to push the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  above the edge of its trading band at 240.01.  \par \par \uc2 With those fears temporarily subdued, the publication of February CPI data on Friday, forecast at 3.8 percent, could still cause a strong market reaction.  \par \par \uc2 Finance Minister Tibor Draskovics said earlier on Thursday that inflation was declining too fast and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  kept higher rates than needed for its own inflation targets.  \par \par \uc2 Lower-than-expected inflation may fuel expectations of sharp interest rate cuts at the end of March and a new forint strengthening towards the top of its trading band at 240.01.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the forint's retreat reduced the chance that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firms to the top of the band in illiquid international trade on Monday and Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 While the NBH probably has the means to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the international market through its agents even if the local market is closed, most traders said it was unlikely to step in before Wednesday's local reopening.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 1615 GMT - EUR/HUF  falls to 243.20/60 from\par 241.61/242.11 USD/HUF       eases to 181.29/93 from 180.82/181.22 3-yr\par 2007/G bond yield up 5 bps at 6.91/7.03 pct 5-yr 2009/D bond yield up\par 12 bps at 6.90/7.00 10-yr 2015/A bond yield up 16 bps at 6.65/6.80pct\par -.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050310e13a00ecy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
