\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Hungary cuts 12-month T-bill auction, yields rise.  \b0\par\par\uc2 347 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2005\par 12:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST, March 10 (Reuters) - Hungary cut its 12-month Treasury bill offer at an auction on Thursday after a forint slide caused a jump in market yields and curbed appetite for the bills, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 The Government Debt Management Agency (AKK) said it sold 24 billion forints ($133 million) worth of the 12-month paper, cutting its offer by six billion forints.  \par \par \uc2 Bids totalled only 30.2 billion forints, compared with a 1.5 bid cover at the previous auction of the 12-month bills held two weeks ago.  \par \par \uc2 The bills were sold at an average yield of 7.05 percent - while the bids accepted spread in an unusually wide range between 6.80 and 7.10 - lower than the previous auction's 7.26 but well above Wednesday's fixing levels at 6.85.  \par \par \uc2 "Looking at the forint levels at the time of the auction, only the particularly courageous went into the auction," one trader said.  \par \par \uc2 The forint fell one percent in early trade to about 244.50 to the euro, sharply reversing earlier gains as foreign investors cut overweight positions in Central Europe's domestic fixed income markets, hitting \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 By 1132 GMT it recovered to 243.25/45.  \par \par \uc2 In Hungary's local market some dealer said it was possible that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBH) stepped in before the fall to curb the earlier forint rises towards to top of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's band at 240.01, but others said \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 12-month Treasury bills usually received less attention than shorter papers. Demand at the auction was even lower than usual, but the reduction in the offer was neither a big surprise nor an upset to the government's financing plans.  \par \par \uc2 "At the earlier auctions this week the AKK raised its offers," one trader said.  \par \par \uc2 The AKK sold 30 billion forints worth of 3-month bills and the same amount of six-month bills this week. It increased its original offers by five billion forints at both auctions.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020050310e13a0099g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
