\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Hungary \highlight\uc2  Ctrl Bk Makes HUF78.5B 03 Net Pft On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 155 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Mai 2004\par 17:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 BUDAPEST (Dow Jones)--The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  made a net profit of 78.5 billion forints ($1=HUF211.32) in 2003 but has no obligation to pay dividends on this profit into the state budget, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  made the profit when it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market last January to weaken the forint after investment banks attempted to push the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the strong end of its trading band.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold forints for close to EUR5 billion and later sold most of the euros at a profit.  \par \par \uc2 In 2003, the bank paid a dividend of HUF23.3 billion into the budget. In 2002 it made a loss of nearly HUF4.9 billion.  \par \par \uc2 -By Balazs Koranyi, Dow Jones Newswires; +361-267-0623; balazs.koranyi@dowjones.com [ 20-05-04 1501GMT ]  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040520e05k000sd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
