\par\par \b \uc2 ANALYSIS-Forint swings add new twist to ERM2 debate.   \b0\par\par\uc2 By James Thornhill   \par \uc2 699 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 November 2003\par 17:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 LONDON, Nov 4 (Reuters) - Market turbulence in Hungary may raise fresh doubts in the European Union about the ability of the future member state to hold its forint within the required bands against the euro before adopting the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 However, some analysts say the turbulence only underlines the advantages of joining the exchange rate mechanism (ERM2), the anteroom for euro zone membership.   \par \par \uc2 The forint and Hungarian government bonds slid sharply on Monday, forcing the Hungarian National Bank to buy bonds in an unorthodox open market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  wants to join ERM2 soon after becoming a full EU member in May 2004 and last month began informal talks with the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (ECB) to discuss that aim and its ultimate goal of euro accession in 2008.   \par \par \uc2 ERM2 locks a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into a central parity rate against the euro and sets 15 percent fluctuation limits above and below that rate.   \par \par \uc2 However, the ECB and EU Commission have said they would prefer the original narrow 2.25 percent bands to be applied for two years when assessing a country's fitness to adopt the euro.   \par \par \uc2 For the original euro founders, the Maastricht treaty stated that a country must observe ERM fluctuation margins for at least two years prior to joining the euro.   \par \par \uc2 "It's important to note that for Hungary the narrow band concept doesn't have any meaning until 2006. So unless you think the 15 percent bands are going to be a problem, there's not necessarily a reason to think ERM2 will be a problem," said Jeff Gable, emerging markets analyst at Deutsche Bank.   \par \par \uc2 FORINT SWINGS   \par \par \uc2 It's not clear whether the idea of early ERM2 entry with a view to waiting several years before joining the euro will be acceptable to euro zone officials.   \par \par \uc2 The Bundesbank in particular has questioned whether early membership of ERM2 is the best option, especially given the problem across eastern Europe of bloated budget deficits.   \par \par \uc2 "Against this background, you have to ask the question whether an early membership in ERM2 makes sense, or whether it it better to wait and reach a higher degree of nominal convergence," Bundesbank Vice President Juergen Stark said in August.   \par \par \uc2 The forint dropped around three percent against the euro in little over a day's trading this week as foreign investors liquidated positions in the local bond market on a spillover of negative sentiment from Poland and Russia.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's credibility also took a knock when it exacerbated the bond market sell-off with a warning that it was prepared to hike interest rates if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to strengthen.   \par \par \uc2 However, it helped calm the market on Monday by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buy government bonds and leaving interest rates on hold at its regular policy meeting, aiding a recovery in the forint.   \par \par \uc2 "There are probably one or two ECB members who are looking at the fiscal numbers and the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility in Hungary and probably shaking their heads," said one London-based analyst.   \par \par \uc2 BETTER INSIDE THAN OUT   \par \par \uc2 In answer to the sceptics within the euro zone, some analysts say entering the ERM2 could be the best way to curb the kind of volatility seen in the forint and the Polish zloty recently.   \par \par \uc2 Ratings agency Fitch, in a report on the 10 EU accession countries on Tuesday, highlighted the potential positive impact of ERM2 membership.   \par \par \uc2 Fitch said ERM2 participants would benefit from the ECB's backing of the system, reducing vulnerability to episodes of financial contagion along the lines seen in Hungary in the past few days.   \par \par \uc2 It also said ERM2 membership would make it more likely that a country meets the euro zone entry criteria and hence joins the bloc on a three-to-four year time horizon.   \par \par \uc2 "The EU needs to ask how \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  volatility and high long-term interest rates help long-term investment and growth...they don't, they're counter-productive," said Charles Robertson, emerging markets analyst at ING.   \par \par \uc2 "This volatility is only hurting Hungary's capacity to join the euro quickly and see real economic convergence...you could argue that it highlights the interests of joining," said Robertson.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031104dzb4003bn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
