\par\par \b \uc2 Polish zloty, bonds claw back losses.  \b0\par\par\uc2 376 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 November 2003\par 16:45\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     WARSAW, Nov 3 (Reuters) - Polish zloty and bonds made back\par ground slowly on Monday, as buyers picked up bargains in the\par country's battered local bonds and Friday's upbeat current\par account numbers played into \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  markets, said dealers.\par     The zloty rose one percent against the euro and 0.3 percent\par versus the dollar, while bond yields fell by up to 15 basis\par points across the yield curve, also aided by a calming in\par sentiment on neighbouring Hungarian markets.\par     Consecutive dives in confidence in Polish and Hungarian\par bonds in recent weeks have pushed yields up by more than 100\par basis points, but some dealers said the tide may have begun to\par turn, with Polish assets now seen as cheap.\par     "We saw foreign banks selling a good quantity of hard\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and there were buyers for the zloty all day long. For\par sure its in part due to a change in sentiment on bond markets,"\par said a dealer with one Warsaw bank.\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     "But it's also due to the fact that fears that we will have\par a further crisis (on the zloty) are fading and the Polish unit\par is regarded as cheap, and well worth buying at its current\par level," he added.\par     In contrast with trade on Thursday and Friday, Polish\par markets were little affected by a nervous morning in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par where the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank intervened\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  via purchases of government\par bonds in a bid to turn around sliding treasury and \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  prices.\par  \par     The fixed-income market likewise showed no reaction to the\par finance ministry's announcement of 1.5 billion zlotys value of\par two-year bond supply tender on Wednesday.\par     "The better mood is a result of a technical correction --\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 we're continuing the trend from Friday's rebound, and the  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 current account numbers have also had a large impact, which we  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 haven't seen in a while," said one fixed income dealer.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 - MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 1529 GMT -  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 EUR/PLN 4.6238 vs 4.6708 at open  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 USD/PLN 4.0200 vs 4.0315  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 2-yr yield (OK0805) 6.51 pct vs 6.55 pct at open  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 5-yr bond yield (PS0608) 6.80 pct vs 6.88 pct  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 10-yr bond yield (DS1013) 6.98 pct vs 7.13 pct  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -.  \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020031103dzb30031m\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
