\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Hungary \highlight\uc2  forint ends firmer on verbal  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 556 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 2003\par 17:31\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BUDAPEST, June 5 (Reuters) - \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's forint was firmer in\par late trade on Thursday after verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  from the\par government and the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (NBH), but remained vulnerable,\par dealers said.\par     The forint                 was quoted at 264.60/265.50 to\par the euro at 1435 GMT or 5.97/6.29 percent above parity in its\par 30-percent-wide band, up from Wednesday's 268.90/269.40 close\par and the day's lows slightly weaker than 270.0.\par     But it retreated from highs at around 263.0, to where it\par surged after Finance Minister Csaba Laszlo said it should firm\par to between 250 and 260 and NBH Governor Zsigmond Jarai said the\par bank would use all its tools to push it to levels around 250.\par  \par     "The verbal \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  had a mixed success, but it's\par unclear how long it can be sustained," one dealer said.\par     "Everybody is watching the impact of a 50 basis point rate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  cut by the ECB (European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ), which has cut fuel for \par \par \uc2  weakening and people also wait for the result of the weekend \par \par \uc2  referendum in Poland (on European Union accession.)" \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Dealers said the forint remained vulnerable to any rise in\par selling pressure in an illiquid market.\par     Foreigners' attitudes will become increasingly important on\par Monday when markets in Hungary are closed for the Pentecost\par holiday, but forint trade in London can continue, dealers said.\par     On the fixed income market, sentiment was jittery with three\par to five year bond yields rising 10-25 basis points, and yields\par in the longest segment up by 5-15 basis points, traders said.\par     "All in all, the market was extremely volatile today, but in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the morning hours there was already some demand for long papers,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par which eventually rescued bonds longer than five years," said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Illes Toth, fixed income analyst at DZ Bank.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said the short end of the yield curve continued pricing\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the possibility of a rate hike and the market was divided\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par over the authorities' forint and interest rate policy.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "As long as the market does not price in the present high \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 FX\f28 \b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par risk, the nervous sentiment will prevail, with the 2-3 year\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par segment looking the most vulnerable," Toth added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par     Other traders also said short-term yields surged by 35-40\par basis points, while losses were smaller at the long end.\par     Analysts have warned that foreign investors were likely to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par place a higher risk premium on their holdings in central Europe\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par after the surprise Hungarian \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  devaluation, though a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sudden stampede from long bond positions was unlikely.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 1435 GMT -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HUF/EUR  264.60/265.50 vs Wednesday 268.90/269.40\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HUF/DLR  up at 223.40/224.25 to from 224.40/225.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 3-yr 2006/F bond yield at 7.05 pct, up about 25 bps\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 5-yr 2008/C bond yield at 6.70 pct, up about 20 bps\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 10-yr 2013/D bond yield at 6.35 pct, up 5-10 bps\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par  --------------------------------------------------------\par     For related news:\par  Hungary Debt                       Hungary \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par  Emerging Market Debt               Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par  All Emerging Markets news          CEE indicators\par  All East Europe News               E.Europe equities\par  TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets\par  TOP NEWS -- Convergence watch\par  Hungary indicators                 Czech indicators\par  Slovak indicators                  Polish indicators\par  Live prices & data:\par  Hungary bonds\par  Central/East Europe Bonds\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Emerging Markets Bonds overview .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030605dz6500ueh\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
