\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary Jarai: Ready To Defend Euro HUF250 Exchange Rate \b0\par\par\uc2  By Balazs Koranyi and Margit Feher \par \uc2 1,485 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 2003\par 10:36\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST -(Dow Jones)- Hungary's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will bring the forint's exchange rate back up to 250 against the euro, even if it takes interest rate hikes or \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Zsigmond Jarai told Dow Jones Newswires Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Jarai was speaking after the authorities unexpectedly devalued the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  Wednesday, cutting the central rate in its trading band by 2.26%, a move which sent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  into a tailspin. \par \par \uc2  It was trading between HUF268-269 to the euro Thursday morning, having weakened Wednesday from HUF255 to HUF270. \par \par \uc2  Jarai said in an interview, however, that the bank is ready to live with a weaker exchange rate for a few days and will stay on the sidelines for now to see how the market settles down. \par \par \uc2  The bank won't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  or raise rates Thursday and will wait for the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rate decision Thursday before assessing its next move, Jarai said. \par \par \uc2  "We want to keep the exchange rate at 250 forints ($1=HUF230.80). We have the tools to keep it there and we're going to keep it there," Jarai said. \par \par \uc2  "If the market prices in a weaker forint, we will react. That could mean a rate hike or that we just won't cut rates after an ECB cut." \par \par \uc2  Jarai admitted that Wednesday's move confused the market and the reaction was more severe than the government had expected. But he stressed that the devaluation didn't mean the bank is ready to sacrifice its inflation targets. \par \par \uc2  "We agreed to the weaker \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  because it doesn't threaten our inflation targets," he said. \par \par \uc2  "We're maintaining those targets and we'll do what it takes to meet them. \par \par \uc2  "The shift in the band limits our maneuvering abilities somewhat but we see that we won't need that room anyway. We can get to the inflation target with the new band just as well," Jarai said. \par \par \uc2  He added that the bank is ready to be more flexible with the target for end-2003 but won't compromise on the end-2004 goal. Jarai sees inflation at the end of this year between 4.5% and 5%, just above the 4.5% target. An exchange rate of HUF250 to the euro will allow end-2004 inflation to be under 4%, Jarai said. The bank's target for end-2004 inflation is between 2.5% and 4.5%. \par \par \uc2  "We won't allow inflation to accelerate as getting it back to lower levels would require too great a sacrifice," Jarai said, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government had made a verbal pact on the shift in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  believes that the move was possible right now because the shift won't compromise our inflation goals," he declared. \par \par \uc2  "The move is a symbolic step on the government's part to exporters that the forint won't strengthen to below HUF240 again," he said. Hungarian exporters have long complained to the government that the strong forint was damaging competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  After the devaluation the forint's strongest spot in the band is now HUF240.01, from HUF234.69. \par \par \uc2  Part of the pact was that the government will reduce public spending this year by HUF74 billion and will remain committed to its 2003 budget deficit target of 4.5% of GDP, Jarai said. The budget deficit was a whopping 9.7% of GDP last year. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said, however, after Wednesday's announcement, that the spending cut isn't substantial and the government will exceed its deficit target regardless. They added that a spending cut in the range of HUF250 billion would have been more reassuring for investors. \par \par \uc2  Jarai stressed that he government needs to remain vigilant in its goal of cutting the budget deficit further and meeting its deficit targets set out in its Pre-Accession Economic Plan submitted to the European Union. \par \par \uc2  The HUF74 billion cut in 2003 spending "is a step in the right direction but further budget adjustments are needed, chiefly to achieve the 2004 budget deficit target," Jarai said. \par \par \uc2  The government aims to reduce the deficit to about 3.0% of GDP in 2004. \par \par \uc2  The verbal pact with the government doesn't include anything about further \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band shifts, Jarai pointed out. \par \par \uc2  But he saw no need for any more such moves, which the market interpreted as a de facto devaluation. They generated a high degree of instability and loss of credibility among investors that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wanted to avoid, he said. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think more shifts will be necessary." \par \par \uc2  The timing of the move was unfortunate since the forint had already weakened to 253-256 against the euro by the time of the announcement, Jarai said. \par \par \uc2  "The decision for the shift wasn't based on the current forint exchange rate," Jarai said. \par \par \uc2  "We won't allow inflation to accelerate as getting it back to lower levels would require too great a sacrifice," Jarai said, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government had made a verbal pact on the shift in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  believes that the move was possible right now because the shift won't compromise our inflation goals," he declared. \par \par \uc2  "The move is a symbolic step on the government's part to exporters that the forint won't strengthen to below HUF240 again," he said. Hungarian exporters have long complained to the government that the strong forint was damaging competitiveness. \par \par \uc2  After the devaluation the forint's strongest spot in the band is now HUF240.01, from HUF234.69. \par \par \uc2  Part of the pact was that the government will reduce public spending this year by HUF74 billion and will remain committed to its 2003 budget deficit target of 4.5% of GDP, Jarai said. The budget deficit was a whopping 9.7% of GDP last year. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said, however, after Wednesday's announcement, that the spending cut isn't substantial and the government will exceed its deficit target regardless. They added that a spending cut in the range of HUF250 billion would have been more reassuring for investors. \par \par \uc2  Jarai stressed that he government needs to remain vigilant in its goal of cutting the budget deficit further and meeting its deficit targets set out in its Pre-Accession Economic Plan submitted to the European Union. \par \par \uc2  The HUF74 billion cut in 2003 spending "is a step in the right direction but further budget adjustments are needed, chiefly to achieve the 2004 budget deficit target," Jarai said. \par \par \uc2  The government aims to reduce the deficit to about 3.0% of GDP in 2004. \par \par \uc2  The verbal pact with the government doesn't include anything about further \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band shifts, Jarai pointed out. \par \par \uc2  But he saw no need for any more such moves, which the market interpreted as a de facto devaluation. They generated a high degree of instability and loss of credibility among investors that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  wanted to avoid, he said. \par \par \uc2  "I don't think more shifts will be necessary." \par \par \uc2  The timing of the move was unfortunate since the forint had already weakened to 253-256 against the euro by the time of the announcement, Jarai said. \par \par \uc2  "The decision for the shift wasn't based on the current forint exchange rate," Jarai said. \par \par \uc2  "We incorporated into the verbal pact that the finance ministry supports ERM II entry as soon as possible," Jarai added. "Prime Minister Peter Medgyessy is inclined towards swift entry." \par \par \uc2  Exchange Rate Mechanism II is a trading band which countries have to join for at least two years prior to euro membership. Hungary plans to join the E.U. in May 2004. \par \par \uc2  "If the 2004 tightening in the budget really takes place as the government promises, the equilibrium exchange rate could be weaker than HUF250," Jarai said, referring to the rate at which the government plans to enter ERM II. \par \par \uc2  Jarai said he doesn't see wages rising more than 5% nominally next year, which is slightly above the bank's projection of 4.1% on average. \par \par \uc2  That fits with recent remarks from Prime Minister Medgyessy who has said public sector wages won't rise faster than inflation. \par \par \uc2  Wages last year rose 18.3% nominally and 13.6% when adjusted for inflation, including sharply steeper rises in the public sector. \par \par \uc2  "Until now we had to have a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  (than HUF250) due to lax fiscal and wage policies...." said Jarai. \par \par \uc2  "But joining ERM II would be worthwhile with a rate close to the equilibrium rate. That rate should be weaker than the average rate of the past two years," Jarai said. \par \par \uc2  Based on the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's annual average exchange rate statistics, the average rate of the past two years is HUF249.83. \par \par \uc2  -By Margit Feher and Balazs Koranyi, Dow Jones Newswires; +361 267 0622; margit.feher@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030605dz65000hw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
