\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Hungary \highlight\uc2  forint extends loss as  \highlight22\uc2 fx intervention \highlight\uc2  ends. \b0\par\par\uc2 473 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 2003\par 10:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, May 29 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forint eased against both the euro and the dollar in the wake of the cental bank's (NBH) Monday "end-of-\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " comment. \par \par \uc2  Bonds also fell, tracking \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market sentiment and German Bund movements and eyeing an auction of three-year bonds . Auctions results are due to be published at 1000 GMT. \par \par \uc2  The NBH said on Monday that it had sold 3.8 billion euros in the market since January, but had now ended \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "With the NBH off the offer for EUR/HUF, we could see spot rise towards 248.00-250.00," said Lehman Brothers in its daily strategy note for central European \b \highlight22\uc2 fx\b0 \highlight\uc2  and fixed income markets. \par \par \uc2  "This is another reason to stay away from the short-end of the bond curve as it may cause market participants to lower expectations of (NBH) base rate cuts," it added. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At 0815 GMT the forint         was quoted at 248.00/20 against the\par euro, or 10.1 percent above parity in its 30-percent-wide flotation\par band, down from Wednesday's close at 246.70/80.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Versus the dollar it traded at 212.00/10, weaker than Wednesday's\par finishing level of 209.80/95.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Trade activity is low as usual, except that the market is now trying\par to put the cross-hair on levels deemed right after the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par comment," one \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  dealer said. - MARKET SNAPSHOT AT 0815 - HUF/EUR\par down at 248.00/20 from 246.70/80 Wednesday HUF/DLR        eases to\par 212.00/10 from 209.80/95 3-yr 2006/F bond yield rises 5 bps to 6.12/20\par pct 5-yr 2008/C bond yield higher by 2 bps at 5.97/6.05 pct 10-yr\par 2013/D bond yield up 3 bps at 5.91/99 pct -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Government bond yields rose around five basis points to track euro zone\par movements, mainly German government securities.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hungary will release first quarter economic growth data on Friday, with\par the year-on-year figure seen dropping to 3.5 percent  from 3.7 in the\par fourth quarter of 2002.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The market will also watch demand at Thursday's auction of 60 billion\par forints ($288.4 million) worth of three-year bonds after recent strong\par oversubscriptions, fixed traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Quite naturally, bonds track German bunds movements, but the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par market's current reactions have also stirred some minds," said Balint\par Kocsis, fixed income trader at Aegon Securities.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par For related news:\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par   Hungary Debt                       Hungary \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par   Emerging Market Debt               Emerging \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \par   All Emerging Markets news          CEE indicators\par   All East Europe News               E.Europe equities\par   TOP NEWS -- Emerging markets\par   TOP NEWS -- Convergence watch\par   Hungary indicators                 Czech indicators\par   Slovak indicators                  Polish indicators\par   Live prices & data:\par   Hungary bonds\par   Central/East Europe Bonds\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Emerging Markets Bonds overview .\par \f28 \par