\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Hungary \highlight\uc2 's c.bank says ends market  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 26 Mai 2003\par 17:06\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, May 26 (Reuters) - The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBH) said on Monday that it had ended \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after selling billion of euros following an inflow of hot money that it fended off in January. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has finished \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  and returns to its earlier practice, in which it influences the exchange rate mainly through its interest rates," the NBH said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  NBH Governor Zsigmond Jarai told a news conference that in January 5.3 billion euros in hot momey flowed into the country due to unjustified speculation that Hungary would lift central parity in the forint's 30-percent-wide band. \par \par \uc2  The NBH cracked down on speculation by buying the euro at the upper end of the band, slashing interest rates and narrowing foreign players' access to its deposit facilities, forcing them to sell their forints at lower exchange rates. \par \par \uc2  The NBH defended the band and has resold 3.8 billion euros through market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  since then, posting a profit of 43 billion forints ($206.7 million), Jarai said. \par \par \uc2  Hot money players lost altogether 240 million euros on winding up their speculative positions, the NBH said. \par \par \uc2  The bank said local investors also posted profits on the speculation as about 1.2 billion euros was rebought by foreign hot money investors from local banks. \par \par \uc2  Jarai said the speculative wave improved the credibility of the NBH's inflation targets instead of breaking the forint band. \par \par \uc2  "It has showed that the bank does everything by using all its tools so as to reach lower inflation levels," he said. \par \par \uc2  The NBH's international reserves fell to 11.562 billion euros by the end of April from January's peak at 14.2 billion. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030526dz5q00t13\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
