\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary's forint bucks easier trend amid rate talk. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sandor Peto \par \uc2 516 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 2003\par 17:22\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, Feb 20 (Reuters) - Hungary's forint bucked a central European trend for easing \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Thursday, closing flat against the euro amid market talk of a possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBH) hike in the overnight deposit rate. \par \par \uc2  Short-term Treasury bill yields rose on the speculation, while government bond yields ticked up slightly amid uncertainty over monetary policy and political tensions over Iraq, shrugging off earlier over-subscribed auctions. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par At 1445 GMT, the forint           was quoted at 246.10/30, or 10.83\par percent above parity in its 30 percent wide trading band, against\par Wednesday's 246.15/30 close. It had earlier dipped to lows near\par 247.00.\par Other central European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  weakened on growing concern over\par possible military action Iraq, with Poland's zloty         falling to\par 32-month lows against the euro.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - MARKET SNAPSHOT AT CLOSE - HUF/EUR  flat at 246.10/30 from\par Wednesday's 246.15/30 HUF/USD        firms to 228.00/20 from 229.50/70\par 10-yr 2007/D bond yield up five bps at 6.37/42 pct 3-mth discount\par T-bill yield up 20 bps at 4.90/5.10 pct\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The forint has found quite strong resistance around 247, while comments\par by Finance Minister Csaba Laszlo triggered expectations for a hike in\par the NBH's overnight deposit rate of 3.5 percent, helping the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ,\par traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Laszlo said on Wednesday that 'hot' money swirling around in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par markets after last month's NBH \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and sharp rate cuts\par hindered an efficient \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 operation\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of financial markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par A closed meeting of NBH Governor Zsigmond Jarai and bankers on Thursday\par added to speculation of a possible overnight deposit rate hike, dealers\par said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The issue discussed could have been that interest rates are low and\par that a small hike would do no harm," one said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par TOUGH TIMES AHEAD\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Most analysts in a Reuters survey on Thursday said the NBH's key\par two-week deposit rate would remain flat for several weeks before a\par hike.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Fresh speculation for a hike in the overnight rate, however, pushed up\par T-bill yields by 20 basis points, while average yields at bond auctions\par  were also higher than forecast.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Traders said the government increased issuing to exploit high market\par liquidity ahead of potentially tough times.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Global sentiment is not too sound, the amounts issued are higher than\par usual and we could see Polish auctions were not too good either," said\par Sandor Jobbagy, fixed income analyst at DZ Bank's regional research\par centre in Budapest.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There's a risk that rate hike expectations resurface and a possible\par Iraq war cuts demand in the future," he added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Andras Laszlo Borbely, Senior Managing Director at the Government Debt\par Management Agency (AKK) said they increased issuing, piling up stocks\par as they did early last year, as yields were lower than a few weeks ago\par and demand quite strong.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "The market is simply good," he said. "If it's not so good later, we\par won't have to accept much if we accept more now."\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030220dz2k01mte\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
