\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary forint down in thin trade, T-bills firm. \b0\par\par\uc2 460 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Februar 2003\par 17:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     BUDAPEST, Feb 14 (Reuters) - Hungary's forint fell in thin\par trade on Friday on small-scale euro orders from commercial bank\par clients, while short-term government paper yields continued to\par fall sharply in a market awash in money, traders said.\par     The forint                 closed at 245.60/80 against the\par euro or 11.52 percent above parity in its 30-percent-wide band,\par down from Thursday's finish at 244.70/80.\par     "It was a very illiquid (\f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 forex\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 ) market which is easy to be\par moved by small amounts," one dealer said. "No direction is seen,\par the forint could move in a range between 244 and 246."\par     The forint settled in that range this week after recent\par volatility amid some long position closing by foreign investors\par to stop losses.\par     But most of the forint funds created by last month's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central\par bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (NBH) \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  are still seeking a home in \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par markets, maintaining an oversupply in money, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     The NBH bought over five billion euros last month to defend\par the top of the forint band at 234.69 versus the euro from a\par speculative attack. It also slashed interest rates and imposed\par restrictions on its two-week deposits, making its low-yielding\par overnight deposits of 3.5 percent its effective key facility.\par     The NBH is expected to keep a 100 billion forint cap on the\par two-week deposits, which yield 6.5 percent, at its weekly tender\par next Tuesday, while government paper worth 190 billion forints\par ($833.2 million) will expire, further boosting liquidity.\par     The oversupply continued to weigh on short-term Treasury\par bills, pushing the three-month yield down by 20 basis points to\par 4.8 percent and the six-month yield 30 basis points to 4.90.\par     But traders said a recent recovery in demand for longer\par maturities was short-lived as a lack of buying interest lifted\par their yields by between five and 10 basis points on Friday.\par  \par     "Next year's bond auctions may be purchased, but I dont't\par expect big demand," one trader said.\par     Analysts were split over the size of bids at next week's\par auctions  where five-year bonds of 40 billion forints\par and 10-year bonds worth 35 billion will be offered.\par     They said general risk aversion by foreigners rose due to\par global political tension, but high market liquidity, coupled\par with low NBH rates, could may lend new strength to bond buying.\par      -----------------MARKET SNAPSHOT AT CLOSE-----------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HUF/EUR  down at 245.60/80 from Thursday's 244.70/80\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par HUF/USD  drops to 226.70/90 fromo 226.00/15\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 3-month D030611 bill yield falls to 4.80 pct\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 5-year 2007/2 bond yield rises five bps to 6.46/50.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030214dz2e00x6x\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
