\par\par \b \uc2  Zloty at 31-mth low vs euro,hedge funds cut exposure. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Wojciech Moskwa \par \uc2 655 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Januar 2003\par 15:19\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  WARSAW, Jan 23 (Reuters) - Poland's zloty fell to a 31-month low versus the euro on Thursday as hedge funds cut exposure to the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after taking losses in neighbouring Hungary, but any further decline was seen limited, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  The zloty has tumbled nearly six percent since \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  slashed interest rates and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market last week to keep the forint from breaching the upper end of its trading band. \par \par \uc2  "This is spillover from Hungary, hedge funds have taken losses there and are reducing positions elsewhere," said Wike Groenenberg, economist at Schroder Salomon Smith Barney in London. \par \par \uc2  The zloty traded at 4.2222 versus the euro and 3.923 against the dollar at 1302 GMT, down 1.3 and 1.0 percent respectively on the day. \par \par \uc2  "We will see further volatility as long as uncertainty in Hungary continues. But when it fades, there may be a buying opportunity," she said, adding that more zloty-bashing by Polish government officials could also unsettle the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The zloty, forint and Czech crown have all benefited from so-called convergence trades, as investors mopped up the region's assets hoping yields would fall in the run-up to European Union entry in 2004 and euro zone membership later in the decade. \par \par \uc2  Negative global sentiment towards emerging markets amid growing uncertainty ahead of a possible U.S.-led war against Iraq has led investors to unwind some of the hefty gains made in the region's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past year. \par \par \uc2  "Once the global market situation stabilises for a bit, we should see the zloty return to its slow upward drift," said Mateusz Szczurek," chief economist at ING Bank Slaski in Warsaw. So far in 2003, the zloty has lost 4.9 percent versus the euro, the forint 5.3 percent and the Czech crown has remained flat, while the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthened nearly 2.5 percent versus the dollar during the same period. \par \par \uc2  VERBAL \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  The zloty, a free floating \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since 1999, also continued to be unsettled by recent comments from Finance Minister Grzegorz Kolodko. \par \par \uc2  Kolodko told Reuters in an interview in Madrid late on Wednesday that "the gradual yet limited depreciation of Polish zloty will continue" in the short-term. \par \par \uc2  Kolodko also reiterated his view that Poland should join the euro zone in four years at a zloty exchange rate of 4.35 to the euro. \par \par \uc2  That has set a target for the volatile market, which had in the past largely ignored government attempts to talk down the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Some players also fretted that the finance ministry had or was on the verge of carrying out an earlier threat to directly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market and sell the zloty. But analysts said any such move, which would be the first by the ministry, would probably not take place until March or April at the earliest, if at all. \par \par \uc2  The ministry has in the past signalled it could go directly to the market to buy hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to finance its foreign debt financing costs instead of dealing with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . While some observers believe the government could carry out this form of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  others say such a move is unlikely since it would probably boost costs at the spend-thrift ministry. \par \par \uc2  Poland's fixed income market also continued to edge lower on Thursday but selling appeared to have run its course, said analysts, with near-term rate cut hopes underpinning prices. \par \par \uc2  Two-year bond yields were up eight basis points to 5.60 percent, while five-year notes were down three points to 5.61 - still a shade above Wednesday's poorly-bid primary tender. \par \par \uc2  Analysts expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 10-member Monetary Policy Council (MPC) to shave 25 basis points from its main rate - now at 6.75 percent - when it meets next week. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030123dz1n00s3l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
