\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Hungary \highlight\uc2  forint eases, cenbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  seen. \b0\par\par\uc2 519 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Januar 2003\par 10:49\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, Jan 21 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forint eased against the euro on Tuesday and a continued fall would likely provoke renewed \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBH) \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to resell part of the billions of euros bought by the bank last week, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "Currently the market is consolidating at lower levels and prices do not move very hectically as there is interest on both sides," said Orsolya Liptai of K&H Bank. \par \par \uc2  At 0850 GMT the forint  was quoted at 246.30/60, or 10.8 percent above parity in its 30-percent-wide band, down from late Monday's 245.40/50. Against the dollar it eased to 231.00/30 from 230.00/30. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said foreign investors were on the selling side, while Hungarian exporters bought the euro, being happy with higher forint revenues after several weeks when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded close to the top of its band at 234.69 versus the euro. \par \par \uc2  However, exporters were unlikely to soak up a big chunk of around 1,000 billion forints ($4.32 billion) sold by the NBH last week to fend off a speculative attack against the band. \par \par \uc2  "If the NBH is consistent, they have to step in again if the forint reaches the 248-250 range," Liptai said. "That's not too far now." \par \par \uc2  The NBH fended off the attack on the band by slashing interest rates and changing its deposit rules to force speculative money to leave the country through the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market. \par \par \uc2  The flight of hot money began on Friday amid high volatility and NBH \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to reverse falls of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The NBH posts gains by selling euros at lower forint levels than 234.69, where it bought the euros. Tuesday is the settlement day of most of last week's euro buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and after a relapse on Monday the market expects continued volatility. \par \par \uc2  With huge amounts of surplus forint liquidity seeking a home in the markets, they will pay close attention to a three-month government bill auction and the NBH's two-week deposit tender later on Tuesday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The government will offer three-month bills worth 25 billion forints, the usual weekly amount. The three-month bill is Hungary's shortest paper and the only one for which demand surged after the hot money outflow began. \par \par \uc2  As part of the measures to scare off hot money, the NBH limited deposits to be accepted at 100 billion forints at its tender, below the usual amount of around 200 billion forints. \par \par \uc2  The overnight interbank money market was in a standstill, with all excess money flowing into the NBH's overnight deposits at 3.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  "Everybody is awash with money and puts it into the NBH. Why should anyone pay more than 3.5 percent now?," said Balazs Hajdu of Commerzbank. \par \par \uc2  Speculators sitting on piles of forint positions, will find no comfort in overnight deposits either as the NBH cut the rate on its only remaining unlimited facility by 400 basis points to 3.5 percent, much below interest rates elsewhere in the region. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030121dz1l00izq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
