\par\par \b \uc2  WRAPUP 2- \highlight22\uc2 Hungary \highlight\uc2  slashes rates,  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  to cool  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sandor Peto and Krisztina Than \par \uc2 931 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Januar 2003\par 19:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, Jan 16 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary authorities fought to hold down the surging forint on Thursday, cutting rates sharply and staging huge market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  within the upper limits of its ERM-2 type system. \par \par \uc2  The Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBH) cut its key interest rates by 100 basis points, the second such slashing of borrowing costs in two days, bringing rates down to 6.5 percent in an attempt to force speculators to abandon upward pressure on the forint. \par \par \uc2  Dealers fled the forint after the rate cut, buying back euro and sending the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  plunging to 250.00 from earlier levels of 234.69, the top of the trading band, where the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively to cool the unit. \par \par \uc2  The sharp cuts bring Hungarian interest rates a quarter point below nearby Poland's. While the cuts may send capital scampering for higher yielding Polish bonds they will make it hard for the NBH to meet its inflation-fighting targets. \par \par \uc2  "They managed to shift the forint from the strong end of the band, but they may have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  tomorrow from the other side," said Istvan Zsoldos of CAIB Securities in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the bank's move to limit the forint deposits it will accept at next week's fixed-rate tender to 100 billion forints ($448.5 million) was key to curbing foreign buyers. \par \par \uc2  "The restriction on deposits will definitely have a strong impact, as it nominally limits the gains on exchange rate speculation," said Dirk Woelfer at S&P MMS in Frankfurt. \par \par \uc2  "Changing the deposit rules was a very smart move," added Orsolya Nyeste at Postabank. \par \par \uc2  CONVERGENCE SPECULATION \par \par \uc2  Foreign capital had poured in to take advantage of Hungary's high rates and its security as a future European Union member. Investors expect interest rates to converge fast with lower euro-land levels, bringing easy profits on government bonds. \par \par \uc2  The speculative inflow has put the NBH in a policy quandary. It has abandoned its opposition to rate cuts to try to hold down the forint, but risks the unit falling to levels that will reignite inflation and put economic stability at risk. \par \par \uc2  "If interest rate levels drop so much that they hit the pain threshold of foreign investors a capital flight can set off, which can make it difficult for the bank to hold the forint at strong levels," said Gyorgy Barcza at ING Bank in Budapest. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the delicate balancing act may be difficult to pull off and signalled the problems future EU members will have trying to find the right level to enter the euro \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if inflation and capital-enticing deficit levels are too high. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  Dealers said the NBH had bought over four billion euros in constant \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  throughout Thursday, the second day it had been forced into the market. \par \par \uc2  Despite the turmoil in the markets \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chief Zsigmond Jarai and Finance Minister Csaba Laszlo said they were determined not to shift the current parameters of the 30 percent trading band. \par \par \uc2  "Today I consulted with Prime Minister Peter Medgyessy and ...Jarai and the common stance of us is: there will not be a band widening or shift," Laszlo said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  Jarai early on Thursday promised interest rate cuts quickly to stem the forint, prompting dealers to say that such a policy would effectively let the market set the price of borrowing. \par \par \uc2  "As market players have realized their power (to change \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy) a renewed attack on the forint can not be excluded at all. Moreover, a nominal key rate at 6.5 percent is still attractive," said Zoltan Torok of Raiffeisen Securities. \par \par \uc2  But NBH determination to put out speculative fires and resist upward forint pressure was underlined by it changing deposit rules and slashing overnight deposit rates to limit the ability of forint holders to find a home for the unit. \par \par \uc2  With falling yields on high-flying government bonds investors left with forint after the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  now have few lucrative places to lodge Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The restriction on deposits will definitely have a strong impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it nominally limits the gains on exchange rate speculation," said Dirk Woelfer of S&P MMS in Frankfurt. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is a lot smarter than the market gave it credit for and policy is now directed solely at burning speculators and ensuring that they don't come back," said one Hungarian analyst. \par \par \uc2  EURO APPROACH \par \par \uc2  The NBH's woes are a precursor of the problems many ex-communist EU members-in-waiting will have as they try to enter the euro, which they are expected to join this decade. \par \par \uc2  Among eight east European states due to join the EU in May 2004 only Hungary is operating an ERM-2 style band system, which all will eventually have to adopt after agreeing parity rates to the euro with the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and EU authorities. \par \par \uc2  The ERM-2 bands are supposed to steady a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it nears euro entry. Hungary's struggle to hold its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down, protecting exporters, underlines the need to choose a credible parity rate that markets will not attack as unacceptably low. \par \par \uc2  Hungary's interest rates had been among the highest among the region's EU designees. \par \par \uc2  They still offer investors a 375 basis point carry over euro zone rates, suggesting speculators will not stay away for long and many analysts believe wealth catch-up and falling inflation also point to a higher forint. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030116dz1g00yw7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
