\par\par \b \uc2  Pressure on forint eases but  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  ongoing. \b0\par\par\uc2 323 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Januar 2003\par 12:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par BUDAPEST, Jan 16 (Reuters) - Upward pressure on \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par forint  continued to force the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to\par sell the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at the top of its band in midday trade on\par Thursday.\par Activity had eased since the morning when investors sold up\par to four billion euros to the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  (NBH), but the bank\par was seen cutting interest rates later on Thursday to avoid being\par forced into further massive \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , dealers said.\par "They have to cut rates and they also said they would," one\par dealer said. "Otherwise someone will ring at their door in the\par morning saying they have brought forty trucks of euros."\par Market players continued to buy forint at the top of the\par 30-percent-wide band at 234.69 against the euro at 1115 GMT, and\par the dollar was also at the edge of the band at 221.90/222.20.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Earlier on Thursday NBH Governor Zsigmond Jarai told a news\par conference that the bank was ready to \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervene\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  and further\par reduce its interest rates after Wednesday's 100 basis point cut\par if large \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 interventions\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  continued to be needed.\par Traders said the market expected a new cut to come later on\par Thursday.\par Jarai, outlining a new NBH strategy amid the heavy capital\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par inflows, said the bank would cut rates to stem speculation but\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par needed the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  to remain near the top of the band to help\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par it defend its inflation targets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par He said the bank needed a strong forint since CPI targets\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par were threatened by the impacts of last years' bloated budget\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par deficit and surging wages.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The governor suggested that interest rates received on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par two-week deposits placed with the NBH by market players who buy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par forint now may be reduced to much lower levels by next Tuesday,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par when the bank reopens its two-week facility to investors.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The facility is open once a week. Jarai's suggestion implies\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par sharp rate cuts before Tuesday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030116dz1g00ngi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
