\par\par \b \uc2  Hungarian Ctrl Bk Sees  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Costs Modest-CSFB \b0\par\par\uc2 342 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Januar 2003\par 13:34\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2003, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST -(Dow Jones)- The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  expects the costs of any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to combat forint strength will be modest, Credit Suisse First Boston said in a research note Tuesday, citing sources at the bank. \par \par \uc2  The sources told CSFB that the bank would be willing to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  at a scale similar to the EUR2.5 billion and EUR3 billion it spent annually between 1996 and 2001, during which time it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  regularly. \par \par \uc2  The bank doesn't expect the amount needed to sterilize the impact of foreign funds will be that high, since the widening of the current account deficit will limit the pressure on the forint to strengthen, CSFB said. \par \par \uc2  However, CSFB believes that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is downplaying the size of any \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and "that hot and convergence money inflows will remain substantial," pushing up the forint. The current account deficit isn't cause for a headache, CSFB added. \par \par \uc2  The Hungarian forint is at record highs, and has been trading close to its strongest level against the euro for several days. The bank allows the forint to trade in a range of plus or minus 15% against the midpoint of its band against the euro. Around 1200 GMT the forint was trading at HUF234.95 ($1=HUF221.96), very close to its strongest level of HUF234.69. \par \par \uc2  The remarks come a day after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left its key interest rate unchanged at 8.5%, surprising economists who expected a cut due to the forint's strength. \par \par \uc2  The decision probably reflects the bank's concerns that it could miss its 4.5% annual inflation target in December, CSFB said. But CSFB sees room for cuts totaling 100 basis points if the upward pressure on the forint persists, in addition to any \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Minister of Finance Csaba Laszlo also said Tuesday that he sees room for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to ease its rates. \par \par \uc2  -By Margit Feher, Dow Jones Newswires; +361-267-0622; margit.feher@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020030114dz1e000sp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
