\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary finmin says strong HUF limits bank's options. \b0\par\par\uc2 286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 2003\par 19:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2003 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, Jan 13 (Reuters) - Hungarian Finance Minister Csaba Laszlo said on Monday the forint's firming to the top of its trading band would limit the independent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (NBH) room for manouevre over monetary policy. \par \par \uc2  Laszlo told Reuters he did not want to comment on the bank's decision earlier to keep key interest rates on hold at 8.50 percent despite the strong forint and market expectations for a rate cut. \par \par \uc2  However, he indicated that continued upward pressure on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could force the bank to cut rates in the near future. \par \par \uc2  "The fact that the forint hit the strong end of its band... signals that the manoeuvring room of the bank's monetary policy will narrow in the future," he said. \par \par \uc2  The bank's decision to leave rates on hold, prompted the forint to rise to the strong end of its 30 percent wide band for the first time since the regime was introduced in May 2001. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said convergence-led capital inflows and speculation about a revaluation of the forint band were likely to keep up the pressure on the band, but the NBH, concerned over inflation, may prefer costly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rate cuts. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans to join the European Union in May 2004 and is eyeing adoption of the euro in 2007. \par \par \uc2  High interest rates have attracted heavy foreign capital inflows into central Europe since late last year. \par \par \uc2  Hungary's forint has also firmed on speculation the bank and centre-left cabinet may have to shift the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's band at some stage, though both have ruled out any change to the current forint regime in the next 18-24 months. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020030113dz1d01174\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
