\par\par \b \uc2  ANALYSIS-Easing,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  won't halt C.Europe  \highlight22\uc2 fx \highlight\uc2  bulls. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Michael Winfrey \par \uc2 850 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 November 2002\par 11:41\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BRATISLAVA, Nov 20 (Reuters) - EU candidates' central banks face a tough fight to contain their surging \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as bullish foreign investors flock to central Europe knowing juicy returns await them when the region joins the euro zone. \par \par \uc2  Polish, Hungarian and Slovak policy makers look destined to repeat the battle waged by the Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which bought billions of euros this year and slashed interest rates below euro-zone levels to stop hot-money inflows pushing up the crown. \par \par \uc2  Like the Czechs, other EU candidates fear that appreciation caused by capital inflows will hit exports and growth as they gear up to join Europe's single market in 2004 and, later in the decade, adopt the euro. \par \par \uc2  Poland, where analysts still see room to ease and pressure on the zloty is not so great, might be able to take a lesson in how the Czechs tamed the crown. But the twin-track defence of rate cuts and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may not work for \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  or Slovakia. \par \par \uc2  Those countries don't have the Czechs' tame inflation and risk stoking price rises if they ease aggressively, while \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  may turn into a blank cheque to speculators. \par \par \uc2  "Is buying a billion euros going to ease the pressure? Two billion? Five billion? Well, if you believe in the convergence play, then no. All it's going to be is a one-way bet for people to play into," said Deutsche Bank analyst Jeff Gable. \par \par \uc2  "Then it becomes a much more difficult choice. If central banks are going to cut interest rates dramatically, then it begins to have implications for their inflationary path." \par \par \uc2  OPENING SHOTS FIRED \par \par \uc2  Investors have rushed to central Europe, where, regardless of fundamentals, they believe debt bought now in future EU members will earn healthy returns as \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  strengthen and the region's interest rates drop to euro-zone levels. \par \par \uc2  Slovakia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fought back last week as foreign inflows pushed the crown to record highs. It bought over 500 million euros over three days and then walloped the market with a 150-basis-point cut in its main rate to 6.5 percent. \par \par \uc2  Hungary followed on Monday with a surprise half-point cut, bringing its key rate to 9.0 percent, as the forint neared the strong end of its 30-percent-wide band against the euro. \par \par \uc2  But the cuts failed to scare away investors, who kept piling on bets that there will be further rate cuts soon, putting the credibility of Hungary's inflation-and exchange rate-targeting regime on the line. \par \par \uc2  Just as in the Exchange Rate Mechanism crises which preceded the creation of the euro, the forint band creates a target which markets can aim at. Only this time, the pressure is on to revalue, not devalue, as Britain and Italy had to in the 1990s. \par \par \uc2  "It's a very difficult situation for the central banks. The question is how far they can go with rate cuts," said Commerzbank's Radomir Jac. "Those we have seen are not working enough to weaken the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ... and even more rate cuts are unlikely to stop the appreciation." \par \par \uc2  The free-floating Slovak crown, which has firmed more than seven percent since July, has returned towards record highs of 41.12 per euro since the rate cut and \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Analysts were unsure as to whether the forint would test the strong side of its band against the euro this year, but noted that the rate cut had not pushed it lower. It was 14.1 percent above its central parity at 237.30 per euro on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  HOW FAR WILL THEY GO? \par \par \uc2  Analysts said Slovakia and Hungary will likely cut again soon if buying persists, but any such move must be backed by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to have any effect. And even then market enthusiasm has a good chance of persisting. \par \par \uc2  "The Czechs only really managed to turn around the crown once their rates were below those of the ECB," said IDEAglobal analyst John Davitte. \par \par \uc2  The Czech \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's two-week repo rate stands at 2.75 percent, 50 basis points below the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's main rate. \par \par \uc2  Davitte said that, with other euro-zone aspirants looking to hit tough targets on inflation and borrowing to qualify for the euro, "I don't think they can afford to cut rates to those kind of levels". \par \par \uc2  Lower rates would mean Hungary's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have to scrap its 2003 inflation target, as the finance ministry has baulked at revaluing the forint band. Rate cuts could also fuel domestic demand in Slovakia and swell an already-wide trade gap. \par \par \uc2  If they feel they can no longer reduce borrowing costs, the banks will be left with only one weapon - \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  - which could result in a long and costly campaign. \par \par \uc2  "It could be that eventually (rate cuts) will stop, and the central banks will have to rely only on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The question then would be whether those would last for a couple of months or even a couple of years," said Jac. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021120dybk00kj4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
