\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1-Hungary PM, c.bank head talk down surging forint. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sandor Peto \par \uc2 558 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 November 2002\par 15:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, Nov 15 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's prime minister and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Friday to talk down the country's soaring \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and the forint retreated a touch from a new record high against the euro. \par \par \uc2  The forint edged down to 237.10/20 following comments by Premier Peter Medgyessy, at a regional summit in Warsaw, and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBH) Governor Zsigmond Jarai. \par \par \uc2  It earlier steamed to a new high of 236.10 to the euro as foreign buyers chased high-yielding interest rates amid speculation the authorities could be forced to raise central parity in the forint's 30-percent-wide flotation band. \par \par \uc2  The top of the band, introduced in May 2001 in preparation for Hungary's eventual entry into Europe's Exchange Rate Mechanism (ERM II), is set at 234.69 against the euro. \par \par \uc2  To defend that, the NBH would have to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  directly by buying euros to weaken the forint. \par \par \uc2  Medgyessy told Reuters on the sidelines of a meeting of European Social Democrat leaders in Warsaw that he wanted to see a realistic exchange rate for the forint, adding he would not move parity in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading band. \par \par \uc2  "The forint should be valued realistically," he said. \par \par \uc2  JARAI SEES NO NEED TO CHANGE PARITY RATE \par \par \uc2  Separately, on the sidelines of a business conference in Budapest, NBH head Jarai said he saw no need to change the parity rate - fixed at 276.10 to the euro last year - before joining the ERM II, a precursor to signing up to the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  euro zone. \par \par \uc2  "We think the forint has come a little bit close to the edge of the band," Jarai said. "I would like to state that under no circumstances will we lift the band... there's no need." \par \par \uc2  "With forint strength within the band we can comfortably meet our end-2003 inflation target (of 4.5 percent)," he added. \par \par \uc2  "If the exchange rate (settles) between 238 and 240, our (end-2003) inflation forecast can change to 4.3 percent (from 4.6), well within the 4.5 percent target," Jarai added. \par \par \uc2  Other central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  have come under pressure as optimism rises over a smooth EU enlargement in 2004. \par \par \uc2  The Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  shocked markets earlier with a 150 basis point interest rate cut to curb its surging crown. \par \par \uc2  "It was mainly Hungarians who were very active in the past couple of hours, but Poles and Slovaks have also been buying (in the forint market)," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  High bond yields, coupled with improved EU entry sentiment, have boosted foreign capital inflows into \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  and fixed income markets. \par \par \uc2  The forint had posted a new euro high of 237.75 on Thursday as government bond auctions attracted strong subscriptions. \par \par \uc2  JP Morgan earlier recommended selling euros and buying forints, saying they offered the best carry trade in central Europe. \par \par \uc2  Hungary's base rate of 9.50 percent is the region's highest. \par \par \uc2  JP Morgan said the forint would remain under upward pressure, which could force the NBH and centre-left cabinet to lift parity, within the next four to six months. \par \par \uc2  HSBC also said the forint rise could force the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band's revaluation by the middle of next year. - Additional reporting by Andras Muller, and Douglas Busvine in Warsaw. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021115dybf00rxm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
