\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Hungary \highlight\uc2  bonds, forint weaken on rate cut,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 364 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Februar 2002\par 17:57\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2002 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, Feb 18 (Reuters) - Hungarian government bonds eased on Monday but activity was limited as investors digested news of a revision to 2001 current account data as well as a 50 basis point rate cut, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The Hungarian forint , which eased after the data revision, weakened further as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  verbally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb a recent rise in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The Government Debt Management Agency (AKK), which fixes yields on benchmark securities once a day at around 1330 GMT, set the yields by up to five basis points higher. \par \par \uc2  The three-year 2005/G was set at 7.44 percent, up four basis points and the five-year 2006/E at 7.19 percent, up three. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said government bonds rose about five basis points after the National Bank of Hungary (NBH) said in the morning that it revised the final current account deficit to 1.262 billion euros from 518 million but eased back later in the day. \par \par \uc2  "Bids inched higher by some five basis points during the day but everybody waited to see what the NBH would do in the afternoon," one government securities trader said. \par \par \uc2  The forint lost ground as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which cut its two-week deposit rate by 50 basis points to 8.50 percent, effective Tuesday, said it did not need a further rise of the forint to meet its inflation targets. \par \par \uc2  The forint eased to 242.00/50 versus the euro by 1620 GMT after 240.20/70 late on Friday, representing a 12.17/35 percent level above parity within its 30-percent-wide trading band. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar it traded at 278.00/55. \par \par \uc2  "What really weighed was the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's announcement that there is no need for further forint strengthening to meet inflation targets," a \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer said. \par \par \uc2  "After this announcement it immediately fell half a forint (against the euro). \par \par \uc2   Latest t-bill auctions..................... \par \par \uc2   Latest bond auctions....................... \par \par \uc2   Forecasts for Hungary econ. indicators..... \par \par \uc2   NBH forint fixings.......... \par \par \uc2   Forint/dollar market quotes. \par \par \uc2   Interbank overnight deposit rates.......... \par \par \uc2   Interbank tomorrow'next deposit rates...... \par \par \uc2   NBH interest rates.......... \par \par \uc2   Benchmark govt securities yields........... \par \par \uc2   Budapest Stock Exchange BUX index........... \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020020218dy2i00yfi\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
