nd yield............\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Planned govt securities auctions...\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  T-bill auctions....................\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Bond auctions......................\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  T-bill prices......................\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Bond prices........................\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Benchmark govt. sec. yields........\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Sovereign issues...................\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Budapest Interbank Offered Rate (BUBOR)...\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ----------- EQUITIES ----------------- -------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Hungarian shares ended higher on Tuesday, with oil and gas\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par group MOL outperfohrming the market on foreign buying ahead of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par an expected decision about the sale of the company's gas\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par division next week, traders said. The BUX index closed at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 6,879.01 points, up by 29.34 points or 0.43 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Hungarian busmaker NABI is expected to post a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par consolidated net income $7.35 million in January-September,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par according to the median forecast of five analysts in a Reuters\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par poll on Tuesday. The figure represents a surge of 156 percent\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par over $2.875 million net profit that NABI posted in the first\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par nine months of 2000.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Hungarian chemicals firm TVK is seen posting weak\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par third-quarter results but sector peer BorsodChem 's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par product structure meant it had better chances to weather a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par downturn in the chemicals cycle.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2