\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary's forint opens firmer as exporters hedge. \b0\par\par\uc2 327 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Oktober 2001\par 09:38\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, Oct 1 (Reuters) - Hungary's forint firmed to 7.2 percent above parity in its band after the opening on Monday, as Hungarian exporters were hedging their foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  revenues with forward transactions, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "Hungarian exporters have been heavily selling foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the past two weeks hedging their revenues with forward deals, which provides support for the forint," said Attila Behan at K&H Bank. \par \par \uc2  On Friday the forint closed at 6.86 percent above central parity in its 30-percent-wide flotation band. \par \par \uc2  Behan said remarks by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor Zsigmond Jarai on Friday that the country did not need to need to change its inflation targets as the forint stabilised after recent falls, had no impact on the forint. \par \par \uc2  Jarai also said that Hungary will not need to take up any new loans from abroad in 2002 to refinance its expiring debt. \par \par \uc2  Against the euro, the forint firmed to 256.20/70 from Friday's close at 256.90/257.00, while against the dollar it traded at 281.80/282.80, easing from 280.90/281.40 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  Behan said the forint would likely trade in a range between 255 and 260 forints to the euro in the near future. \par \par \uc2  He said the termination of the forint's crawling peg devaluation system on Monday had no significant impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Hungary on Monday ended the forint's crawling peg devaluation system, as one of the last steps of a monetary overhaul in its run-up to European Union membership and the forint's joining the euro zone. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBH) set the forint at the middle of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band at 276.1 forints per euro. \par \par \uc2  The forint now floats in a 15 percent-wide range on either side of this parity. Hungary expects to join the EU in 2004 and the eurozone about two years later. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020011002dxa103r1q\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
