\par\par \b \uc2  Hungarian Forint Slide Leaves  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  In A Quandary \b0\par\par\uc2  By Margit Feher \par \uc2  Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES \par \uc2 778 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 September 2001\par 17:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST -(Dow Jones)- The National Bank of Hungary finds itself in a policy quandary. \par \par \uc2  Just as the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy board prepares to meet on Monday, the forint has fallen through a key support level against the euro, a victim of the mounting global tension which is souring sentiment in emerging markets. \par \par \uc2  The move took the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to more than HUF260 against the euro on foreign selling in late afternoon trade Friday. That's the weakest it's been since May, and it's expected to weaken further next week. \par \par \uc2  "We broke an important support," said Zoltan Szabo at WestLB in Budapest. "Liquidity is pretty low since it's a Friday afternoon. Next week (when trade picks up) I see some further weakening. The forint could fall to 262-263." \par \par \uc2  Investors are now looking to the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  for action. \par \par \uc2  There's been no sign of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, dealers said. \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  executives have been unavailable to comment. \par \par \uc2  "The National Bank is keeping quiet. It should raise interest rates, I think," Szabo said. \par \par \uc2  "But it just lowered them last week. They're just thinking very hard right now about what to do." \par \par \uc2  At around 1200 GMT, the forint was trading at HUF260.80-20 or 5.5% on the strong side of its trading band, weaker than HUF258.00-30, or 6.5% on the strong side of its band, in the morning. \par \par \uc2  "HUF260 was a great watershed, foreigners are selling forints and buying euros," said a dealer at Raiffeisen. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allows the forint to trade in a plus or minus 15% band around a midpoint it sets daily against the euro. \par \par \uc2  But its current level is far from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's target of HUF245-250, which it set to reduce annual inflation in December to 7%, down from 10.1% in December 2000. \par \par \uc2  More encouragingly, meanwhile, local bonds are faring much better than the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The amount of Hungarian bonds in foreign hands has been mostly steady since last Tuesday, even slightly higher, at around HUF950 billion, data from the state debt management center AKK show. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                       Sound Economy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hungary's economy is sound, with inflation on a downward path. But the\par gathering global crisis, following last week's atrocities in the U.S.,\par has driven investors into the safest boltholes, such as U.S. short-term\par debt.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Stock markets, meanwhile, have suffered agonizing selloffs throughout\par the world and many emerging market \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , such as the forint, have\par been exchanged for safer bets like the Swiss franc, which is at a record\par high against the euro.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par In such conditions, a rise in rates to support the forint would make\par the bank look to be out of control and smack of economic mismanagement.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Only last week the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut its key rate by 25 basis points to\par 11%, citing, among other factors, an earlier 25 basis point cut by the\par European \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 . However, a bank executive said Tuesday it won't\par immediately follow this week's 50 basis point cut by the ECB.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The most likely outcome is for the bank to stand pat in view of the\par weak forint, though most analysts see more rate cuts to come this year\par on the back of slowing inflation.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Credit Suisse First Boston economist Istvan Racz takes that line. He\par sees unchanged rates Monday but a good chance of a quarter-point cut\par 10.75% at some point in October.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "This could take place if, as we and the market expect, there's a\par further drop in year-on-year inflation to 8.1% in September from 8.7% in\par August," Racz said in a research note Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Rate cuts will likely total 50 basis points altogether for the rest of\par the year as fiscal policy will get considerably looser and inflation\par will only fall moderately in the fourth quarter, Racz added.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Investors must also keep an eye on general elections in neighboring\par Poland over the weekend.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Unlike the forint, the Polish zloty firmed markedly Friday, but\par experience shows that the forint and the zloty often correlate as both\par are 'emerging Europe' \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 .\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "Next to the (sometimes) close correlation in the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currencies\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , the\par issue of European Union accession deserves special attention in the\par Polish elections," Hungarian retail bank IE-New York Broker said in a\par research note Friday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Hungary and Poland plan to be among the first countries to join the\par E.U. sometime after 2004.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Margit Feher, Dow Jones Newswires; +361-267-0622;\par margit.feher@dowjones.com (Balazs Koranyi contributed to this item.)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010921dx9l000xn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
