\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Hungary \highlight\uc2  forint opens flat, averts  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  risk. \b0\par\par\uc2 421 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 Juli 2001\par 02:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, June 2 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forint was steady against its flotation band in early trade on Monday as no news provided it with new fuel to restart its recent rally, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  so as to curb the forint's strength after the forint retreated from record highs on Friday and stayed at the lower levels. \par \par \uc2  "(Preliminary May) current account data will come out tomorrow, and a lot will depend on them," one dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The forint traded at 11.1 percent above parity in its 30-percent-wide flotation band at 10:20/0820 GMT, steady from Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  Against the euro it eased to 243.75/95 from 243.20/80, while versus the dollar it softened to 288.60/289.00 from 287.40/90. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  retreated in profit-taking on Friday, after rises to record highs at above 11.7 percent last week despite warnings from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it was too strong. \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  also confirmed last week that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  only if the forint reaches the top of the band. But dealers still saw a risk that the bank steps in earlier to prevent an advance of the forint to the edge of the band. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said on Monday that the forint's retreat temporarily averted the risk of a market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed nine percent within the band since May 4 when the band was widened to 15 percent either side of a daily-set central parity rate, from 2.25 percent. \par \par \uc2  Dealers did not exclude that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  may strengthen further this week. Current account data may give indications to the market, they added. \par \par \uc2  Analysts' consensus forecast for the May current account deficit was 90 million euros in a recent Reuters survey. \par \par \uc2  May was the first month when the strengthening forint began to make imports cheaper and exports more expensive, but analysts said any impact on data would appear with a delay of months. \par \par \uc2  However, the poll conducted two weeks ago also showed that most analysts did not expect a deterioration in the current account despite the strong forint. \par \par \uc2  The forint floats in a 15-percent-wide range on either side of a parity rate set daily by the National Bank of Hungary against a euro curency basket. From April 1, 2001, the forint is devalued every working day at a 0.2 percent monthly rate. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010912dx7200dk2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
