\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Hungary \highlight\uc2  cbank-forint too strong, no  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  yet. \b0\par\par\uc2 193 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 2001\par 02:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, June 27 (Reuters) - The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBH) said on Wednesday that the forint was too strong but there would be no open-market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  before it hits the strong end of the band at 15 percent above parity. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  but believes the forint is too strong," NBH spokesman Gabor Missura told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "The present exchange rate of the forint is already (firm) enough to meet the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's inflation target," he added. \par \par \uc2  "There is no internal band," Missura said, referring to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stance - voiced when the band was widened on May 4 - that the bank would not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  unless the forint hits the strong end of the band at 15 percent above parity. \par \par \uc2  This was the second verbal warning from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , after last Friday NBH deputy general manager Zsolt Ersek said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  should not firm further after a recent rally lifted the unit more than nine percentage points in its new 30-percent-wide flotation band. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday at 0800 GMT the forint traded at 11.21 percent above midline. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6r00onl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
