\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary's forint ends at record-high 11.60/70 pct. \b0\par\par\uc2 373 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 2001\par 17:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, June 27 (Reuters) - The Hungarian forint closed at a new all-time high at 11.60/11.70 percent above parity in its trading band on Wednesday and was seen firming further in a bullish market, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "There is unbroken optimism in the market," a dealer said. "The forint may zig-zag a bit in the next few days but will likely hit the strong end of the band soon," he added. \par \par \uc2  After a slight easing in the morning on euro buying due to usual end-of-month payments of energy bills, the forint resumed its firming trend in the afternoon, undeterred by a second verbal warning from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that it was "too strong." \par \par \uc2  The forint closed at 242.30/50 versus the euro, firming from 243.10/30 on Tuesday, while against the dollar it finished at 281.60/90, compared with 281.90/282.00 on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  On Tuesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at 11.36 percent above the midline in its 30-percent-wide flotation band. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the forint may strengthen in the medium term, unless the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  decides to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBH) said on Wednesday the forint was too strong but there would be no open-market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  before it hit the strong end of the band at 15 percent above parity. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  but believes the forint is too strong," NBH spokesman Gabor Missura told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  "The present exchange rate of the forint is already (firm) enough to meet the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's inflation target," he added. \par \par \uc2  But on Tuesday analysts said the NBH might be forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to stop the forint strengthening further if verbal warnings did not do the trick. They said an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would probably come when the forint hits around 13 percent above midline in the band. \par \par \uc2  The forint floats in a 15-percent-wide range on either side of a parity rate set daily by the National Bank of Hungary against a euro curency basket. From April 1, 2001, the forint is devalued every working day at a 0.2 percent monthly rate. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6r00ryb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
