\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary forint firms by midday,seen climbing further. \b0\par\par\uc2 410 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 2001\par 02:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, June 25 (Reuters) - The Hungarian forint firmed to 11.50 percent above parity in its flotation band by 1145 GMT on Monday, up from 10.73 percent above midline in early trade, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  They said a slight weakening of the forint at the opening was due to the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's verbal \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  late on Friday. However, the easing was only temporary and dealers said they expected the Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to climb even higher in the band in the rest of the week. \par \par \uc2  "The forint has strengthened again since the morning on continued foreign buying," Attila Behan at K&H Bank said. \par \par \uc2  "Neither Friday's verbal statement nor this morning's news that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  would buy 2.9 million euros every day had any impact on the market," Behan added. \par \par \uc2  The NBH said on Monday it would buy a total of 366 million euros this year on \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to meet foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  need linked to the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  denominated debt of the public sector. But the bank said the move was not intended to influence the short-term movements of the forint's exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  At 1145 GMT the forint traded at 242.80/243.10 against the euro, compared with 244.15/35 late on Friday and 244.80/245.00 in early trade on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar the forint traded at 282.10/40, firming from 284.90/285.00 in early trade and 284.67/285.07 on Friday. \par \par \uc2  The NBH on Friday verbally \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in an effort to prevent the forint from a further strengthening. \par \par \uc2  But dealers said only a drastically unfavourable inflation figure or some harder measure by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could stop the forint from rising further in the band. \par \par \uc2  The Central Statistical Office (KSH) is due to release June inflation data on July 11. \par \par \uc2  The forint has firmed more than nine percentage points within its trading band since its flotation band was widened to 15 percent either side of a central parity on May 4 from 2.25 percent, as part of a general overhaul in the monetary system. \par \par \uc2  The forint floats in a 15-percent-wide range on either side of a parity rate set daily by the National Bank of Hungary against a euro curency basket. From April 1, 2001, the forint is devalued every working day at a 0.2 percent monthly rate. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6p00xh0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
