\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary forint rises ahead of full convertibility. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Sandor Peto \par \uc2 533 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Juni 2001\par 02:00\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, June 15 (Reuters) - Hungary's forint extended its gains on Friday, the last trading day before full convertibility. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said further rises may come next week and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may be prompted to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We expect the authorities to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  verbally shortly so as to stabilise the forint around the current levels at 10 percent (above parity in the trading band)," said Istvan Racz of Credit Suisse First Boston. \par \par \uc2  The government published a decree on full forint convertibility on Friday, removing restrictions on short-term capital flows. The move had been widely expected but it does not come into force until Monday. \par \par \uc2  The forint closed at 10.2/10.3 percent above parity in its 30-percent-wide flotation band, retreating from the day's peak at 10.45 percent or 245.55 against the euro, but well up from Thursday's finish at 10.0 percent above midline. \par \par \uc2  It strengthened to 245.90/246.20 against the euro from 246.00/80 and to 284.55/90 against the dollar from 290.20/40. Government bonds firmed in the early afternoon on a buying wave by foreigners encouraged by liberalisation, but returned to earlier levels amid profit-taking in late trade. \par \par \uc2  The main question about near-term market movements is whether foreign capital pours into the market in one wave after it is freed up on Monday, or comes in gradually, dealers said. A surge might be followed by corrections, they added. \par \par \uc2  Opinions were mixed but most market participants expected liberalisation to lift the forint early next week. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said liberalisation would also lead to a surge in turnover but London may benefit more than Budapest. \par \par \uc2  "I fear most of the trade will go to London," one delaer said. "Foreigners will determine the market and if they can trade among themselves they will do that - we can't do anything against that." \par \par \uc2  FORINT SEEN UP, \b \highlight22\uc2 INTERVENTION\b0 \highlight\uc2  A QUESTION \par \par \uc2  Analysts said liberalisation was likely to boost the forint further to levels around 12 percent above parity. \par \par \uc2  "I expect the forint to peak at 12 percent at the strongest," said Kornelius Purps of HypoVereinsbank. \par \par \uc2  "After that, and this process might start already on Monday afternoon, the forint is expected to weaken to levels below 10 percent," he added. \par \par \uc2  Purps said the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBH) was unlikely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  because the forint was affected by one-off factors, adding that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could step in only if the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  settles at levels far above 10 percent in two weeks time. \par \par \uc2  Marton Nagy of ING Investment said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would retreat after peaking at 11-12 percent above parity next week, also pushed down by probable NBH interest rate cuts in line with falls in inflation from July. \par \par \uc2  Gabor Bekes of Lehman Brothers said the forint was unlikely to rise above 11 percent next week but if it continues to firm, the government or the NBH would warn of its strength. \par \par \uc2  A money market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and even interest rate cuts by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , however, were unlikely until the forint reaches 13-14 percent above parity in the band, Bekes added. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6f01n6u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
