\par\par \b \uc2  TUESDAY IN BRIEF - Hungary - Feb 23. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,115 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 2000\par 08:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2   * The U.S. Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) plans to \par \par \uc2  expand its Budapest \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  this spring in an effort to \par \par \uc2  combat Russian organised crime, U.S. officials said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2   * Hungary is doubling security for a friendly soccer match \par \par \uc2  against Australia on Wednesday in case angry fans throw dead \par \par \uc2  fish at the visiting team, Hungarian officials said on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2   * Hungary's state-owned national railway company MAV and its \par \par \uc2  rail unions signed a labour pact on Tuesday following the end of \par \par \uc2  the nation's longest rail strike, the MTI news agency said. \par \par \uc2  -------- FORINT ----------------------------------- \par \par \uc2   * Hungary's forint closed slow trade sharply lower against its \par \par \uc2  flotation band on Tuesday following press reports that the \par \par \uc2  National Bank of Hungary (NBH) favoured a weaker forint, dealers \par \par \uc2  said. The forint ended at 1.55 percent above parity in the \par \par \uc2  4.5-percent-wide band, recovering from a low at 1.45 percent, \par \par \uc2  but well down from Monday's end at 1.90 percent. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2  ended at 257.25/60 against the dollar, up from Monday's finish \par \par \uc2  at 260.45/75, while versus the euro it fell to 257.70/258.00 \par \par \uc2  from 256.50/75. \par \par \uc2   * The National Bank of Hungary (NBH) has told commercial banks \par \par \uc2  that it may take measures to cut the forint's strength, \par \par \uc2  countering speculation in favour of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Hungarian \par \par \uc2  pa