\par\par \b \uc2  WEDNESDAY IN BRIEF - Hungary - Feb 3. \b0\par\par\uc2 551 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Februar 2000\par 06:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2   * Standard & Poor's (S&P) upgrade of Hungary's long-term \par \par \uc2  foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt to BBB+ from BBB on Wednesday is justified \par \par \uc2  by the country's economic performance, and further upwards \par \par \uc2  revisions are seen following, analysts said. \par \par \uc2    --------- FORINT ----------------------------------- \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  * The Hungarian forint\tab     closed firmer, at the strong end\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of the 4.5-percent-wide \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 intervention\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  band, helped by \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Hungary\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par upgrade by Standard & Poor's, dealers said. On Tuesday the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par forint ended at 2.20 percent above the midrange. Against the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par dollar, the forint ended at 262.86/96, down from 261.75/90 at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Tuesday's close. Against the euro it ended at 255.35/40, barely\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par changed from 255.40/45.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Forint/dollar quotes...............\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  forint fixings........\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  --------- INTEREST RATES, BONDS ----\tab     ----------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Hungarian government bond prices were firmer on Wednesday,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par though they gave up some of the early gains made after Standard\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par & Poor's upgraded Hungary's foreign debt rating to triple "B"\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par plus from triple "B", traders said. They said bond yields were\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par five basis points below late Tuesday's levels after falling\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par about 10 basis points after the announcement.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * The average annual yield on Hungary's six-month discount\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par treasury bills was set by auction at 10.81 percent on Wednesday,\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par down from 10.97 percent set at an auction two weeks ago, the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Government Debt Management Agency (AKK) said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Hungary's overnight interest rates ended steady at 11.75/12.00\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par percent on Wednesday and are seen staying close to these levels\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the next few days, dealers said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  O/N rates..........................\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  T/N  rates.........................\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  NBH repo/reverse repo rates........\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  NBH one-year bond yield............\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Planned govt securities auctions...\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  T-bill auctions....................\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Bond auctions......................\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  T-bill prices......................\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Bond prices........................\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Benchmark govt. sec. yields........\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Sovereign issues...................\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Budapest Interbank Offered Rate (BUBOR)...\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ----------- EQUITIES -----------------\tab     -------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * The upgrade of Hungary's debt by Standard & Poor's (S&P)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par boosted Budapest stocks on Wednesday, but they closed only\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par slightly higher, weighed on by selling of oil group MOL shares\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par and uncertainty on global markets. The BUX index closed higher\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par by 0.42 percent or 40.00 points at 9,623.36 points, retreating\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par from the day's peak at 9,817.76.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Hungarian drug shares outperformed the market on Wednesday as\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par some investors actively bought Richter  shares ahead of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the release of the firm's 1999 earnings later this week.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Hungarian axle-maker Raba  said on Wednesday that it\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par was considering a financial bail-out to troubled steel-maker\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Diosgyori Acelmuvek (DAM), one if its largest suppliers.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  All BSE funds......................\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Index to Hungarian company RICs....\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Diary of Hungarian shareholders....\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Net loss leaders.. ..   BUX index..............\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Pct gain leaders....    Pct loss leaders.....\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  OTC weekly turnover................\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  CESI Central European Share Index..\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ----------- COMMODITIES -------------\tab     ----------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Hungarian grains futures closed mixed on Wednesday with market\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par participants taking a wait-and-see attitude in the absence of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par fresh market-moving news, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - ECONOMIC INDICATORS - -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Hungary's current account data due on Thursday, a day after a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ratings upgrade, could confirm Hungary's leading position in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Centr