\par\par \b \uc2  EMERGING MARKET  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Rebound as Latam worries ease. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,004 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Juli 1999\par 13:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, July 14 (Reuters) - Emerging market \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  rebounded on Wednesday as the latest flurry of Latin America worries appeared to ease. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that took a knock earlier this week on talk that Argentina might not service its debt were mostly firmer, with the Polish zloty and South African rand showing the clearest recovery. \par \par \uc2  Emerging Asian units saw a more muted reaction but held up well despite substantial sell-offs on regional stock markets and tension between Taiwan and China, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  Taiwanese stocks plunged nearly four percent on Wednesday, rattled by Taipei's break with the "One China" policy that had helped smoothe relations with Beijing, but traders said the stand-off was partly used as an excuse to take profits. \par \par \uc2  South Korean stocks closed 3.4 percent down and Hong Kong's Hang Seng index lost nearly three percent. \par \par \uc2  "We're moving into a corrective phase for Asian stocks, which is not surprising given the huge gains since the beginning of this year," said Mitul Kotecha, emerging markets economist at Standard Chartered in London. \par \par \uc2  "That, and growing concern on competitiveness, will filter into the \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ' performance at some point, and should prevent further appreciation in the near term. But the medium-term trend is to strength." \par \par \uc2  The Taiwan dollar was little affected by the China tensions, but South Korea's won slipped as local banks bought dollars to meet a government deadline on loan loss provisions. \par \par \uc2  Latin American stock markets stabilised on Tuesday and \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  recouped much of their lost ground. \par \par \uc2  Most analysts were already seeing this week's Latin America-inspired sell-off as vastly overblown when the man largely responsible for triggering the panic, Argentine presidential candidate Eduardo Duhalde, denied late on Tuesday he had ever called for a debt pardon. \par \par \uc2  Kotecha said \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the rand, Indonesian rupiah and Philippine peso, which are underpinned by investors seeking high yield, had been hardest hit by the Latin America jitters as players fled to safer havens such as U.S. Treasury bonds. \par \par \uc2  The rand bobbed back on Wednesday, although it was still some way off the levels of around 6.1 to the dollar seen at the end of last week, and far from the 6.0 mark tested in late June. \par \par \uc2  The Polish zloty, often the Central European \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  most vulnerable to wider emerging market sentiment, jumped to open at 5.62/5.58 percent above its basket parity from late Tuesday's 5.03 percent. \par \par \uc2  The Slovak crown also rebounded sharply, helped by comments by the European Union's executive body that it expected the country to be admitted to formal EU membership talks at the end of this year. \par \par \uc2  But the Czech crown was more subdued, dipping after a local newspaper quoted an unnamed \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  board member as saying he was in favour of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forint, largely insulated by its semi-convertible status from the Latin America worries, showed no reaction to Tuesday's 25-basis-point cut in the two-week repo rate. \par \par \uc2  "To some extent it was expected," said Jan Pudil, a local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt trader at Westdeutsche Landesbank's emerging markets division in London. \par \par \uc2  "It just paves the way for a further easing. The real level of interest rates is so excessively high compared to other countries in the region." \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the strength of the forint was the main factor behind the easing, despite \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  worries about the government's fiscal policies and strong import demand. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been pushing at the top end of its tight 4.5 percent-wide trading band for well over a month, requiring frequent \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  to keep it in check. \par \par \uc2  "Continued large-scale capital flows into the country will provide new impetus for the discussion (at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and between the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the government) on the future shape of the exchange rate regime," Salomon Smith Barney analyst Wike Groenenberg said in a briefing note. ** Following is a table of key emerging market exchange rates, including the change versus late New York trade the previous day and the change in the year to date.. ** The Czech, Polish, Hungarian and Slovak \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , formerly quoted against the mark, are now quoted against the euro to reflect new market norms. All other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are quoted against the dollar. ** According to market convention, exchange rates are quoted in units per dollar or euro and the percentage change denotes the rise or fall of the dollar or euro value. ** Annual percentage changes are calculated from late on the first day of the current trading year, January 4. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCY\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab \tab     LATEST  PREV    PCT CHG  PCT CHG\par \tab