\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary forint eases vs band on commercial orders. \b0\par\par\uc2 281 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 April 1999\par 14:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, April 12 (Reuters) - Hungary's forint ended morning trade weaker on Monday, at parity in the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (NBH) 4.5-percent-wide \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, pushed down by small-scale commercial orders, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "This is (banking) customer business," said Gabor Butor of Raiffeisen-Unicbank, adding that foreigners showed little interest after a general rally in the country's markets on Thursday and early Friday. \par \par \uc2  The forint began to ease Friday amid profit-taking after a rally triggered by Thursday's better-than-projected current account data and the NBH's return to its interest rate cut policy which was expected by some analysts to boost foreign investors' confidence. \par \par \uc2  The NBH cut its benchmark rates by 50 basis points early Friday. The forint closed on Friday at 0.35/0.4 percent above parity. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the forint may firm a little in the afternoon as a correction of the fall, but will stay close to parity. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar the Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  finished morning trade at 234.65/75, slightly firmer than Friday's close at 234.90/235.20, while versus the euro it it softened to 254.80/255.00 from 253.10/60. \par \par \uc2  The NBH fixed the forint at noon at 235.10 to the dollar an at 254.75 to the euro. \par \par \uc2  The forint fluctuates by 2.25 percent on either side of a parity rate set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  according to the value of a basket of 30 percent dollars and 70 percent euros. \par \par \uc2  ((Sandor Peto, Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4044 budapest.newsroom@r