\par\par \b \uc2  Hungarian forint eases vs band after profit-taking. \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 April 1999\par 13:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, April 12 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's forint opened easier against the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band on Monday in slow trade, due to \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying following profit-taking in the country's markets late Friday, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  "I can imagine that (banks) who remained short on Friday are closing positions now," one dealer said. "But turnover is very low, almost nothing happens." \par \par \uc2  The forint was quoted at 0725 GMT at 0.12 percent above parity in the 4.5-percent-wide \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  range, compared with 0.35/0.4 percent above mid-line at Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  The forint began to ease Friday afternoon amid profit-taking in the country's markets after a general rally following better-than-expected current account data released on Thursday and a 50-basis-point \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate cut Friday morning. \par \par \uc2  The rate cut was expected by some analysts to help restore foreign investors' confidence in the Hungarian economy after earlier current account and budget figures triggered concerns. \par \par \uc2  Since the initial rally on Friday, Hungarian markets have become calm again and foreigners are showing little activity, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the forint was expected to move in a narrow range around parity on Monday. \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar the Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at 234.70/235.30, compared with Friday's end at 234.90/235.20, while against the euro it eased to 254.30/255.00 from 253.10/60. \par \par \uc2  The forint fluctuates by 2.25 percent on either side of a parity rate set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  according to the value of a basket of 30 percent dollars and 70 percent euros. \par \par \uc2  ((Sandor Peto, Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4044 budapest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv4c0340a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
