\par\par \b \uc2  WEEKEND IN BRIEF - Hungary - April 12. \b0\par\par\uc2 1,185 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 April 1999\par 07:34\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2   * The Hungarian government agreed a target on Saturday of \par \par \uc2  growth in gross domestic product of 4.5 percent and an inflation \par \par \uc2  target of six to seven percent for the year 2000. \par \par \uc2   * Hungarian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and capital markets burst higher and then \par \par \uc2  saw a round of profit-taking on Friday as caution re-appeared \par \par \uc2  despite a surprise cut of key interest rates and the release of \par \par \uc2  strong current account data. \par \par \uc2   * The National Bank of Hungary's (NBH) rate cuts on Friday \par \par \uc2  after Thursday's good current account data are seen dismissing \par \par \uc2  much of the concerns over the economy and boosting the country's \par \par \uc2  markets, analysts said. \par \par \uc2  ----------FORINT------------------------------------ \par \par \uc2   * The forint closed at 0.35 to 0.40 percent above parity within \par \par \uc2  the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (NBH) 4.5 percent wide \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, slightly below Thursday's close at 0.5 \par \par \uc2  percent above parity but significantly weaker than Friday's \par \par \uc2  opening level of 0.85/95 above mid-line. \par \par \uc2   * The forint ended higher against the dollar at 234.90/235.20 \par \par \uc2  compared with Thursday's close at 235.65 but was little changed \par \par \uc2  against the euro at 253.10/60 compared with 253.40 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  --------- INTEREST RATES -----------\tab     ----------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  * The National Bank of Hungary (NBH) cut its three benchmark\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rates by half a percentage point on Friday, with an immediate\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par effect, the NBH said in a statement.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  * The National Bank of Hungary (NBH) sliced half a percentage\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par point off key interest rates on Friday in a move analysts said\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par should ease concerns over the economy and boost the country's\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par markets.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  * Hungarian bonds rallied on Friday in high turnover and active\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par foreign investor interest in a market that has struggled since\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par early February, traders said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  * Hungarian overnight rates finished lower on Friday after the\par \f28 \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  cut its three benchmark interest rates by 50 basis\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par points, dealers said. Overnight interest rates ended at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 15.375/15.50 percent, compared with Thursday's close at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 15.625/75 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  O/N rates..\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  T/N  rates..\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  NBH repo/reverse repo rates.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  NBH one-year bond yield.....\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  T-bills auctions..   to\tab \par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  T-bill prices............\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Bonds.....\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Benchmark govt. sec. yields...........\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Sovereign issues......\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Budapest Interbank Offered Rate (BUBOR)...\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ----------- EQUITIES -----------------\tab     -------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Hungarian shares ended one percent higher on Friday with late\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par session profit-taking shouldering aside a surge at the open\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par following the announcement of February current account data and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  rate cut.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * The rise leaves the index 5.9 percent higher this week, with\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par most gains realised on the back of the expectations of the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par favourable current account figures.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * The BUX index closed 1.02 percent or 59.45 percent higher at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 5,836.80 points, down from an open of nearly three percent up.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Spot share turnover on the Budapest Stock Exchange rose to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 20.723 billion forints ($95.71 million) on Friday from 15.566\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par billion forints on Thursday, the Budapest Stock Exchange said in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a statement.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Hungarian canned food maker Globus Konzervipari Rt\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par said on Friday it planned to pay a dividend of 150 forints/share\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par on its 1998 results, as compared to a dividend of 130\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par forints/share last year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  All BSE funds.....\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Index to Hungarian company RICs.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Diary of Hungarian shareholders.....\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Net loss leaders.. ..   BUX index..............\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Pct gain leaders....    Pct loss leaders.....\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  OTC weekly turnover..\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  CESI Central European Share Index....\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ----------- COMMODITIES -------------\tab     ----------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Grains futures on the Budapest Commodity Exchange (BCE)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par remained virtually unchanged on Friday but traders expected\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par prices to continue this week's falling trend due to a Danube\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par block which would hinder exports.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - ECONOMIC INDICATORS - -\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par * Hungary's \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  sees year-on-year inflation falling to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par as low as 8.5 percent by December and could cut real interest\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par rates further after Friday's 50 basis points reduction, a senior\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par bank official said. ----------- ENERGY\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -------------------   ----------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  ------------OTHER HUNGARY NEWS-------------------------------\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Hungarian diary......\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Hungarian events diary.............\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Hungarian Press Digest.............\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     ***DOMESTIC POLITICS, GENERAL NEWS***\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     ALL PAPERS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     - Hungary will not fix refugee quotas and is ready to\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par provisionally receive all those whose lives are in danger, Prime\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Minister Viktor Orban said on Thursday. He also said he expects\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par a long war in Yugoslavia.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - Yugoslavia aims to join the federation of Russia and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Belarus, Gennady Selezhnov, speaker of the Russian Duma, said at\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Ferihegy airport on Thursday. He also said that at present\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Moscow is studying means of Russian-Yugoslav cooperation in\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par military technology.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - Foreign Minister Janos Martonyi spoke in Luxembourg on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday of plans to build an air corridor between Hungary and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par the Albanian capital of Tirana, as well as the extension of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par humanitarian aid for victims of the conflict in Kosovo.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - Workers' Party president Gyula Thurmer declared sympathy\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with his host Yugoslav President Slobodan Milosevic at a meeting\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in Belgrade on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - The cabinet will submit to Parliament a reworked version\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of a package of bills aimed at combatting organised crime. The\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par cabinet also decided to upgrade personal documents. It was also\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par declared that the Health Ministry, given the choice among\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par medicines with identical effective agents, will subsidise those\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par medicines that it considers best.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - The present three-week cycle of sessions in Parliament\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par will not change, House Speaker Janos Ader made it clear at a\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par meeting on Thursday.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - A total of 800 properties will be returned to the\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par ownership of the Hungarian Catholic Church by 2011. Minister of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par National Cultural Heritage Jozsef Hamori said Parliament has set\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par aside five billion forints for restoring ecclesiastical\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par properties to their former owners this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - The Trade Union of Interior Ministry Workers decided on\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Thursday to set up a strike committee on May 1 in a bid to press\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par home its wage demands.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     - Hungary and Romania plan to open three new border stations\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par in the next four years.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     NEPSZABADSAG\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     - NATO has taken control of temporarily designated parts of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par around half of Hungarian air space, based on the authorisation\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par of Parliament, Janos Fulop, department head at Air Traffic and\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Airport Directorate said.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     ***BUSINESS AND FINANCE***\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     ALL PAPERS\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     - Preliminary data by the National Bank put the current\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par account deficit for February at $64 million, to give a total of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par $239 million for the first two months of this year.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     - A decision was finally reached on Thursday to go ahead\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par with the issue of the new seven-year global bond, but to a total\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par value of $500 million instead of the $750 million originally\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par planned.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - Agriculture Minister Jozsef Torgyan declared on Thursday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par he had "already signed a decree stating that pork may not be\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par procured for less than 193 forints per kilogram, regardless of\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par quality".\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par MAGYAR HIRLAP\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - After a break of two months, the State Debt Management\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Agency auctioned 10-year bonds again on Thursday, to a total\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par value of 10 billion forints.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - Workers at BorsodChem decided at a meeting on Thursday\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par that if no agreement can be reached with regard to wage\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par increases by April 20, a warning strike will be called.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     - Tinned food producer Globus has signed a supply contract\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par worth five to six million German marks with NATO.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     NAPI GAZDASAG\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     - Last year the Matra Power Station increased profits by\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par over 32 percent.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par     ((Budapest newsroom ++ 36 1 327 4040\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par budapest.newsroom@reuters.com)).\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (C) Reuters Limited 1999.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv4c033px\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
