\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary forint ends weaker against band. \b0\par\par\uc2 383 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 1999\par 13:42\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, April 9 (Reuters) - Hungary's forint closed weaker on Friday within the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket as profit-taking trimmed early gains inspired by a good current account figure, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "There was profit-taking as those who opened long positions when the forint was around parity (within the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's basket) closed them now," said Balazs Benczedi of WestLB Hungaria. \par \par \uc2  The forint closed at 0.35 to 0.40 percent above parity within the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (NBH) 4.5 percent wide \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, slightly below Thursday's close at 0.5 percent above parity but significantly weaker than Friday's opening level of 0.85/95 above mid-line. \par \par \uc2  "A similar profit-taking happened in government securities, and equity purchases (by foreign investors) could not compensate for that," Benczedi said. \par \par \uc2  The forint ended higher against the dollar at 234.90/235.20 compared with Thursday's close at 235.65 but was little changed against the euro at 253.10/60 compared with 253.40 on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Benczedi said that the weakening of the forint was probably temporary and it should rise again early next week. \par \par \uc2  "Friday is a short trading day and the atmosphere was more suited for profit-taking, but the forint should strengthen next week, because confidence is returning," he said. \par \par \uc2  The forint opened stronger against the band at 0.7 percent above parity after the NBH cut its benchmark rates by 50 basis points in the morning. \par \par \uc2  A rate cut can normally ease a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by reducing the demand of foreigners for government securities, but analysts said the NBH's move could increase confidence in the economy and could trigger capital inflows. \par \par \uc2  Hungary's markets have been depressed for months due to investors concerns over the budget and current account deficit. \par \par \uc2  The NBH released good current account data on Thursday, showing a preliminary accumulated deficit of $239 million, compared with analysts' average forecast of $340 million. \par \par \uc2  The forint fluctuates by 2.25 percent on either side of a parity rate set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  according to the value of a basket of 30 percent dollars and 70 percent euros. \par \par \uc2  ((Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4042 budapest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv4903a47\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
