\par\par \b \uc2  Forint may be pressured if c/a data unfavourable-Nomura. \b0\par\par\uc2 261 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 15:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, March 5 (Reuters) - The Hungarian forint may attract some pressure next week if January current account data, due on Monday, are unfavourable but it is unlikely to suffer an attack, Nomura Research said. \par \par \uc2  "The forint...is likely to see further pressure if Monday's current account figures are unfavourable," London-based analysts said in Nomura's "Emerging European Daily" report dated March 4. "However, we do not expect any substantial fall in the forint. \par \par \uc2  The forint ended on Friday at 0.25/0.3 percent below parity in the 4.5-percent-wide \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, up from Thursday's close at 0.7/0.8 below parity on what some dealers attributed to market talk that the current account data will be good. \par \par \uc2  The data will be released after market close on Monday, at 1500 GMT. \par \par \uc2  Market participants have said the forint could fall to the bottom of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, where the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBH) sells foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , if the January current account deficit is higher than the consensus forecast of $290 million. \par \par \uc2  But Nomura said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  proved itself willing to defend the forint's narrow band in the wake of the Russian crisis last year. \par \par \uc2  "The market will be unwilling to re-test the NBH as their \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and higher interest rates were painful to those who bet against the forint last year," the analysts said. \par \par \uc2  ((Sandor Peto, Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4044 