\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary forint steady vs band, shrugs off debt rise. \b0\par\par\uc2 182 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 Februar 1999\par 10:12\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, Feb 23 (Reuters) - Hungary's forint opened steady against the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's basket on Tuesday, shrugging off Monday's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announcement of an $834 million December rise in the country's net foreign debt, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The forint opened at 1.25 percent above parity within the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (NBH) 4.5-percent wide \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band, virtually unchanged from Monday's close of 1.23 percent above parity. \par \par \uc2  The Hungarian unit was also little changed against the dollar at 227.20, compared with Monday's close of 227.15/45. It also held its position versus the euro at 250.45/65, compared with Monday's close of 250.30/70. \par \par \uc2  The forint can fluctuate by 2.25 percent on either side of a parity rate set by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  according to the value of a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket made up of 70 percent euros and 30 percent dollars. \par \par \uc2  ((Denes Albert, Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4042 budapest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dv2n041ll\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
