\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary  \highlight22\uc2 central bank \highlight\uc2  says won't widen forint band. \b0\par\par\uc2 247 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Januar 1999\par 18:55\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, Jan 22 (Reuters) - The National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  (NBH) does not intend to widen the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band in which the forint floats, NBH Deputy Governor Gyorgy Szapary said on Friday. \par \par \uc2  "Today we have no intention whatsoever to expand the exchange rate band because we think once something is functioning well, we don't have to repair it," Szapary told journalists at a Budapest conference on the euro \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Hungary. \par \par \uc2  "The system has operated well, is operating well and we have no intention to change it for the time being," he said. \par \par \uc2  Some analysts have suggested in recent weeks that the National Bank of Hungary should and could widen the 4.5-percent-wide forint band to give the bank greater ability to use monetary policy and cut the costs of maintaining the current band. \par \par \uc2  The Hungarian government initiated a "crawling peg" exchange rate mechanism in 1995 which allows the forint to fluctuate by 2.25 percent on either side of a parity rate set by the national bank and devalued by 0.6 percent each month. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  floats against a basket comprised of 30 percent dollars and 70 percent euros. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been trading close to the strong end of the band since early-December after falling to the weak end during the Russian financial crisis. ((Daniel Langenkamp, Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4043 budapest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000