\par\par \b \uc2  Hungarian Forint Weakens Further To 0.4% On Trading Band \b0\par\par\uc2 307 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 1999\par 15:01\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1999, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST (Dow Jones)--The Hungarian forint is falling further Wednesday afternoon following its steep morning losses in its trading band, with more declines expected on worries over Brazil's economic health. \par \par \uc2  Around 1340 GMT, the forint was at 0.4% from the midpoint on the strong side of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's trading band, down from around 1.5% at 1015 GMT and also down from 2.25% late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allows the forint to move a maximum of 2.25% from the midpoint, which is fixed using a basket of 30% dollar and 70% euro. The bank devalues the forint by 0.6% each month against the basket. \par \par \uc2  "This doesn't seem to be the end," said Istvan Hideg, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at Erste Bank Hungary in Budapest. "The forint may not stop falling until it's at the midpoint." \par \par \uc2  However, Hideg didn't rule out a more severe weakening that would push the forint into the weak side of the band. The forint last traded in the weak side in mid-December. \par \par \uc2  Despite the sharp fall of the forint, the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market, and dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  probably won't step in unless the forint appears likely to hit the weakest side of the trading band. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman declined to comment on Wednesday's developments. \par \par \uc2  Around 1340 GMT, the dollar was at HUF217.15-217.35, up from HUF216.24-216.44 at 1015 GMT and also higher from HUF216.25-216.45 in late trading Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The euro was at HUF255.20-255.58, up from HUF253.23-253.58 at 1015 GMT and higher from HUF249.25-249.45 late Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 13-01-99 \par \par \uc2  1401GMT \par \par \uc2  1168 1868 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010826dv1d00a1r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
