\par\par \b \uc2  Hungary forint ends higher vs band, dollar. \b0\par\par\uc2 184 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Dezember 1998\par 16:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  BUDAPEST, Dec 21 (Reuters) - The Hungarian forint closed significantly higher against the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket helped by good macroeconomic news but also a very low turnover on the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, traders said on Monday. \par \par \uc2  "The forint rose some two percent within the basket since last Wednesday," said Gabor Butor of Raiffeisen Unicbank. \par \par \uc2  On Monday the forint closed at 1.75 percent above parity within the National Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Hungary\b0 \highlight\uc2 's (NBH) 4.5 percent wide \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  band compared with .075 percent above parity at Friday's close. \par \par \uc2  But Butor said part of the rise was due to the fact that the market became one-sided, with virtually no demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "This is a highly illiquid market...and a two percent rise in three days is too much," he said. "This can only really happen in emerging markets." \par \par \uc2  Against the dollar, the Hungarian unit closed at 213.50/70 compared with Friday's close of 215.00/10. \par \par \uc2  ((Budapest newsroom +36 1 327 4042 budapest.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926ducl0200f\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard